## 📊 What is Percentile?

A **percentile** tells us the value below which a certain percentage of observations fall.

For example:

- 25th percentile → 25% of the data is below this value
- 50th percentile → 50% of the data is below this value
- 90th percentile → 90% of the data is below this value

## 📈 What are Quartiles?

Quartiles divide an ordered dataset into **four equal parts**.

| Quartile | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Q1 | 25th percentile |
| Q2 | 50th percentile / Median |
| Q3 | 75th percentile |

### Interquartile Range (IQR)

The IQR measures the spread of the middle 50% of the data.

**Formula:**

```text
IQR = Q3 - Q1
